12
00:56:00,000 --> 00:56:06,000
Bolt is a 2008 American animated adventure comedy film
produced by Walt Disney Animation Studios.

13
01:00:40,000 --> 01:00:46,000
It was directed by Chris Williams and Byron Howard, written by Williams and Dan
Fogelman, and features the voices of John Travolta and Miley Cyrus.

14
01:05:20,000 --> 01:05:26,000
The film's plot centers on a dog named Bolt (Travolta), who has spent his entire life on
the set of a television series and firmly believes that he has superpowers.

15
01:10:00,000 --> 01:10:06,000
Bolt premiered at the El Capitan Theatre in Hollywood, Los Angeles, on November 17, 2008, and
was released in the United States on November 21, by Walt Disney Pictures.

16
01:14:40,000 --> 01:14:46,000
The film received positive reviews from critics and grossed
$310 million against a $150 million budget.

17
01:19:20,000 --> 01:19:26,000
It is regarded as helping to instigate a rebirth of Walt Disney Animation Studios, setting the studio in a new
creative direction that led to other critically acclaimed features such as Tangled (2010) and Frozen (2013).

18
01:24:00,000 --> 01:24:06,000
The film was nominated for several awards, including the Academy Award and the Golden Globe
for Best Animated Feature, and Golden Globe Award for Best Original Song.

19
01:28:40,000 --> 01:28:46,000
The film explores themes of hamster, human animal
relationship, talking dog, animals, cat vs dog.

20
01:33:20,000 --> 01:33:26,000
The tone is lighthearted.
